  "extra_findings": [
    "F3 — listing/search shows every client's tickets to any logged-in user (index.php:72-73); real violation of the manifest's visibility rule outside the ?ver IDOR row",
    "F4 — CSV export (index.php:44-47) hands every ticket to any logged-in client",
    "F11 — exportarCsv leaves a full copy of all tickets at EXPORT_DIR/chamados.csv (inside the web tree) after every export (lib.php:125-150)",
    "F12 — fixed export file name: concurrent exports truncate/mix each other, fopen/query failures return silently, PHP 8.4 fputcsv deprecation notice (lib.php:126-135); a different defect from BUG-004's handle leak",
    "F14 — no login rate limiting / brute-force protection (index.php:20-29)",
    "F15 / ARCH-003-like — no layer encodes the visibility policy; $uid/$papel computed and unused (index.php:38-39)",
    "F16 — array GET/POST parameters (busca[]=, login[]=) cause TypeError and HTTP 500 (index.php:22, :72-73)",
    "F17 — connect_errno check is dead code on PHP >= 8.1 (mysqli throws), uncaught exception instead of the intended message (index.php:9-12)",
    "F19 — exportarCsv mixes query, formatting, disk I/O and HTTP, and depends on the EXPORT_DIR global from config.php (lib.php:123-151)",
    "F20 — session lock held for the whole request serialises same-session requests (index.php:15)",
    "F21 — mediaResposta pulls every answered row into PHP just to sum it (lib.php:109-115)",
    "F23 — formatarStatus returns 'Resolvido' for any status outside 1..3 (lib.php:26-35); contracted behaviour kept (rule 14)",
    "F24 — rotuloPrioridade labels an unanswered priority-4 ticket 'Aguardando 1a resposta' (lib.php:56-58); contracted behaviour kept (rule 14)",
    "F25 — no logout and no absolute session expiry; role frozen in session (index.php:24-25, :38-39)",
    "F26 — listing has no pagination and leading-wildcard LIKE forces a full scan (lib.php:78-85); explicitly not an 'add an index' claim",
    "PERF-002 — SELECT * in listarChamados/exportarCsv noted inside F13 and in Decisions (lib.php:80, :132)",
    "SEC-005 — no CSRF on the login POST, listed as a recommendation in Decisions"
  ],
